records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-04/2026-07-04t23-31-12z-statbel-cpi-headline-yoy-2026-07/raw_response.txt:1:{"slug":"belgium-cpi-annual-rate-july-2026","country":"EA","type":"data","title":"Belgium CPI inflation, July 2026","question":"Statbel Belgian headline consumer price index annual inflation rate for July 2026, not seasonally adjusted, first official print","unit":"percent","pointEstimate":3.2,"ciLow":2.4,"ciHigh":4.1,"confidence":0.8,"resolutionDate":"2026-07-30","resolutionSource":"Statbel Consumer Price Index - Health Index release","resolutionSourceUrl":"https://statbel.fgov.be/en/themes/consumer-prices/consumer-price-index","resolutionRule":"Resolve to the first Statbel-published annual inflation rate for the Belgian headline Consumer Price Index for m-2026-07, reported in percent and rounded to the agency's published precision; do not use later revisions or mirrors.","dataPointId":"statbel.cpi.headline_yoy.2026-07.first_print","historicalContext":[{"label":"2026-06 headline CPI inflation","value":3.4},{"label":"2026-05 headline CPI inflation","value":4.08},{"label":"2026-04 headline CPI inflation","value":4.01},{"label":"2026-03 headline CPI inflation","value":1.65},{"label":"2025-07 headline CPI inflation","value":1.92}],"drivers":["June headline inflation fell from May but remained above the 13-month average","Energy inflation was still positive but eased in June","Food inflation was near zero and pulls down the July base case","Services and rents remain sticky upside pressure","July travel and holiday components can add seasonal volatility"],"sourceContext":["https://statbel.fgov.be/en/themes/consumer-prices/consumer-price-index","https://statbel.fgov.be/en/calendar","https://bestat.statbel.fgov.be/bestat/crosstable.xhtml?view=31b8021d-3fcd-4a8b-ac49-92beabf434e9"],"runAt":"2026-07-04T23:31:20Z","reasoning":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Belgium July 2026 Headline CPI Inflation Forecast"},{"kind":"text","text":"The resolver is the first Statbel print for Belgian headline CPI annual inflation for July 2026, not a HICP flash estimate and not a revised database value. Statbel defines inflation as the ratio of the CPI for a month to the CPI for the same month one year earlier."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked Statbel release calendar for the target month and publication date.","result":"The official calendar lists Consumer Price Index - Health Index for m-2026-07 on 30 July 2026."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the latest Statbel CPI release page for recent headline CPI inflation and index levels.","result":"For June 2026, Statbel reported headline inflation at 3.40%, May at 4.08%, April at 4.01%, March at 1.65%, CPI index 102.95 in June, and CPI index 103.26 in May."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the latest Statbel release details for components and monthly movements.","result":"June 2026 CPI fell by 0.31 points or 0.30% month on month; health-index inflation was 2.99%, core inflation was 3.04%, energy inflation was 10.31%, food inflation was 0.06%, services inflation was 5.10%, and rent inflation was 3.38%."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the official be.STAT table for the 13-month annual-inflation reference class.","result":"The be.STAT last-13-month global headline inflation values include July 2025 at 1.92%, January 2026 at 1.10%, April 2026 at 4.01%, May 2026 at 4.08%, and June 2026 at 3.40%."},{"kind":"text","text":"The base rate/reference class from the last 13 official monthly headline prints averages about 2.33%, but the latest 3 prints average about 3.83%. I weight the near-term state more heavily because the April-June regime includes the current energy and services configuration, while keeping the longer reference class as a pull toward lower inflation."},{"kind":"math","text":"Prior/update/interval: Start with a June persistence prior of 3.40% and a latest-3-month state anchor of 3.83% against a 13-month historical sample mean of 2.33%; update by -0.25 pp for easing energy from 11.20% in May to 10.31% in June and by -0.10 pp for food at 0.06%, offset by +0.10 pp for services at 5.10%, rents at 3.38%, and July travel seasonality. Rounded point = 3.20%. The 80% interval uses recent first-print monthly volatility around persistence, widened for July energy/travel swings, giving 2.40% to 4.10%."},{"kind":"text","text":"Upside risk: renewed electricity, gas, motor-fuel, air-ticket, or package-holiday increases could keep the annual rate near May's 4.08% or would land above the interval if they combine with stronger services. Downside risk: another June-like monthly CPI decline, weaker fuel prices, or broader goods discounts could push the print below 2.40% outside the interval."},{"kind":"forecast","point":3.2,"ciLow":2.4,"ciHigh":4.1}]}
