 headline CPI annual inflation for July 2026, not a HICP flash estimate and not a revised database value. Statbel defines inflation as the ratio of the CPI for a month to the CPI for the same month one year earlier."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked Statbel release calendar for the target month and publication date.","result":"The official calendar lists Consumer Price Index - Health Index for m-2026-07 on 30 July 2026."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the latest Statbel CPI release page for recent headline CPI inflation and index levels.","result":"For June 2026, Statbel reported headline inflation at 3.40%, May at 4.08%, April at 4.01%, March at 1.65%, CPI index 102.95 in June, and CPI index 103.26 in May."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the latest Statbel release details for components and monthly movements.","result":"June 2026 CPI fell by 0.31 points or 0.30% month on month; health-index inflation was 2.99%, core inflation was 3.04%, energy inflation was 10.31%, food inflation was 0.06%, services inflation was 5.10%, and rent inflation was 3.38%."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the official be.STAT table for the 13-month annual-inflation reference class.","result":"The be.STAT last-13-month global headline inflation values include July 2025 at 1.92%, January 2026 at 1.10%, April 2026 at 4.01%, May 2026 at 4.08%, and June 2026 at 3.40%."},{"kind":"text","text":"The base rate/reference class from the last 13 official monthly headline prints averages about 2.33%, but the latest 3 prints average about 3.83%. I weight the near-term state more heavily because the April-June regime includes the current energy and services configuration, while keeping the longer reference class as a pull toward lower inflation."},{"kind":"math","text":"Prior/update/interval: Start with a June persistence prior of 3.40% and a latest-3-month state anchor of 3.83% against a 13-month historical sample mean of 2.33%; update by -0.25 pp for easing energy from 11.20% in May to 10.31% in June and by -0.10 pp for food at 0.06%, offset by +0.10 pp for services at 5.10%, rents at 3.38%, and July travel seasonality. Rounded point = 3.20%. The 80% interval uses recent first-print monthly volatility around persistence, widened for July energy/travel swings, giving 2.40% to 4.10%."},{"kind":"text","text":"Upside risk: renewed electricity, gas, motor-fuel, air-ticket, or package-holiday increases could keep the annual rate near May's 4.08% or would land above the interval if they combine with stronger services. Downside risk: another June-like monthly CPI decline, weaker fuel prices, or broader goods discounts could push the print below 2.40% outside the interval."},{"kind":"forecast","point":3.2,"ciLow":2.4,"ciHigh":4.1}]}
