a June persistence prior of 3.40% and a latest-3-month state anchor of 3.83% against a 13-month historical sample mean of 2.33%; update by -0.25 pp for easing energy from 11.20% in May to 10.31% in June and by -0.10 pp for food at 0.06%, offset by +0.10 pp for services at 5.10%, rents at 3.38%, and July travel seasonality. Rounded point = 3.20%. The 80% interval uses recent first-print monthly volatility around persistence, widened for July energy/travel swings, giving 2.40% to 4.10%.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Upside risk: renewed electricity, gas, motor-fuel, air-ticket, or package-holiday increases could keep the annual rate near May's 4.08% or would land above the interval if they combine with stronger services. Downside risk: another June-like monthly CPI decline, weaker fuel prices, or broader goods discounts could push the print below 2.40% outside the interval.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":3.2,\\\"ciLow\\\":2.4,\\\"ciHigh\\\":4.1}]}\"}}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-04/2026-07-04t23-31-12z-statbel-cpi-headline-yoy-2026-07/codex_events.jsonl:21:{\"type\": \"item.completed\", \"item\": {\"id\": \"item_9\", \"type\": \"agent_message\", \"text\": \"{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"belgium-cpi-annual-rate-july-2026\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"EA\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Belgium CPI inflation, July 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Statbel Belgian headline consumer price index annual inflation rate for July 2026, not seasonally adjusted, first official print\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"percent\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":3.2,\\\"ciLow\\\":2.4,\\\"ciHigh\\\":4.1,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-07-30\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"Statbel Consumer Price Index - Health Index release\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://statbel.fgov.be/en/themes/consumer-prices/consumer-price-index\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first Statbel-published annual inflation rate for the Belgian headline Cons