ction.json:2152616:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Policy and measurement mechanism: the target is a household-survey unemployment rate, not a claimant-count or payroll series. Soft PAYE and vacancies tend to lift unemployment with a lag, but seasonal-adjustment review and LFS sampling variability can move the first print by several tenths without a true labour-market break.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152620:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152621:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152628:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152629:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152632:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The UK labour market is currently one of the clearest stress points: unemployment is up, payroll employment is falling, and wage growth remains central to Bank of England decisions. This target resolves on 2027-02-16 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~2 weeks lag. The same series can also spawn next release, quarterly path, claimant threshold questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152636:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152637:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152640:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"This mirrors the Manifold-style Q4 target: a one-decimal ONS LFS unemployment rate for October-December 2026. The agent keeps the central path near 5.1%, consistent with a labour market that weakens through mid-2026 but stabilizes rather than deteriorating sharply by year-end.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152644:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152645:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152652:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152653:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152656:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"UK unemployment rate, October to December 2026\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152660:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152661:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152668:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152669:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152676:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152677:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152684:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16.4\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152685:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152688:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Counter-consideration: the outcome falls below 4.4 if labour demand re-accelerates and the 2025 unemployment rise unwinds quickly; it exceeds 5.9 if payroll weakness turns into a recessionary hiring stop or LFS volatility prints another sharp unemployment jump.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152692:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16.5\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152693:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-oct-dec-2026.2026-06-16T10-20-43Z.thesis-analyst-live-2026-06-16\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152712:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"PAYE payrolls are a timely administrative labour-market signal, often cleaner for near-term movement than the survey unemployment rate. This target resolves on 2026-06-18 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~2 weeks lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, labour-market threshold questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152828:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152829:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152836:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152837:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152840:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The unemployment rate is the fastest official read on Canadian labour-market slack and feeds directly into household-income, poverty, and Bank of Canada predictions. This target resolves on 2026-06-05 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~1 day lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, rate-decision reaction questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152844:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152845:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152848:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The April rate rose to 6.9% while employment was little changed for a second month after a weak February. The agent centers May at 7.0% because participation and job-search behavior can keep unemployment elevated even if employment does not fall sharply.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152852:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152853:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.canada-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2152872:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Employment change is a high-cadence calibration target for labour income, payroll tax bases, and poverty forecasts. This target resolves on 2026-06-05 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~1 day lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, unemployment threshold questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153164:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153165:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153172:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153173:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153176:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The unemployment rate is a central near-term input for Australian monetary policy, household-income forecasts, and benefit-pressure predictions. This target resolves on 2026-06-25 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~3 weeks lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, RBA reaction questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153180:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153181:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153188:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153189:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-04T11-36-25-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153196:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-20T09-10-00-04-00.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-brier-shadow-no-packs.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153197:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-20T09-10-00-04-00.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-brier-shadow-no-packs\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153204:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-20T09-10-00-04-00.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-brier-shadow-no-packs.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153205:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-20T09-10-00-04-00.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-brier-shadow-no-packs\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153208:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The control run persists April's rounded unemployment rate and gives one to two ticks of household-survey noise.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153212:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-20T09-10-00-04-00.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-brier-shadow-no-packs.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153213:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-20T09-10-00-04-00.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-brier-shadow-no-packs\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153220:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.