\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153253:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153256:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The resolver is the ABS Labour Force, Australia May 2026 release, using the seasonally adjusted national unemployment rate on the first official print. The ABS publication page says the May 2026 release is scheduled for 25/06/2026 at 11:30am AEST, so the resolution date is 2026-06-25.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153260:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153261:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153264:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Base-rate/reference-class: adjacent-month Australian unemployment prints usually move by 0.0 to 0.2 percentage points at one-decimal precision outside shocks. The latest four seasonally adjusted prints, 4.1, 4.3, 4.3, and 4.5, imply a level around the mid-4s, while the April trend estimate of 4.3 suggests not all of the April spike should be extrapolated.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153268:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153269:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153272:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Counter-consideration: April could mark genuine labour-market weakening, with employment down 18,600 and unemployed people up 33,000, so a further increase to 4.6 or 4.7 is plausible. Against that, hours worked rose 16 million and participation slipped to 66.7%, so the unemployment rate may stabilize rather than keep rising immediately.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153276:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z.4\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153277:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153284:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z.5\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153285:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-03-58Z.australia-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-03-58z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153304:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Employment change is a fast, noisy target that helps calibrate household income, tax receipts, and welfare-demand predictions. This target resolves on 2026-06-25 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~3 weeks lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, unemployment threshold questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153336:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The control run mean-reverts April's employment decline toward trend without using unemployment, hours, or claims-style cross-checks.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153408:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Counter-consideration: April's unemployment-rate rise to 4.5% and the ABS note that May has two incoming rotation groups raise downside and survey-volatility risk, so I keep a wide interval that includes another negative employment change.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153568:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Inflation is still above target and trimmed mean remains elevated, while the unemployment rise argues against over-tightening. The agent centers on a hold, with the main tail being a 25 basis point increase rather than a cut.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153756:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153757:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153764:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153765:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153768:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Euro area unemployment anchors labour-income, social-benefit, fiscal, and monetary-policy forecasts across member states. This target resolves on 2026-07-02 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~1 month lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, slack threshold questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153772:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153773:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153776:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Monthly euro area unemployment has been stable around 6.2%-6.3% even as inflation and growth risks shifted. The agent centers May at 6.3% and keeps the interval tight because one-month changes in the harmonised rate are usually one tenth or less.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153780:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153781:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153788:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153789:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153792:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Euro area unemployment rate, May 2026 first print\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153796:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153797:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153800:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The target is Eurostat's first official May 2026 euro area seasonally adjusted unemployment rate, total sex and age 15-74, in percent. The April 2026 Eurostat release states the next unemployment release is on 2 July 2026, so that is the verified resolution date for the May 2026 first print.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153804:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153805:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153808:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Base rate/reference class: monthly euro area unemployment rates usually move slowly at one-decimal precision; the last five official points shown for the euro area are 6.3, 6.3, 6.4, 6.3, and 6.3, making 6.3 the modal and median recent print.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153812:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.3\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153813:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153820:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.4\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153821:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153824:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Counter-consideration: Q1 GDP contraction of 0.2%, weaker retail trade, and higher May inflation at 3.2% could weaken demand and push unemployment up. These forces justify keeping upside mass at 6.4-6.5 rather than making the interval too narrow.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153828:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.5\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153829:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153832:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Use recent monthly persistence as the anchor: median(6.3, 6.3, 6.4, 6.3, 6.3) = 6.3. Apply no directional adjustment because the April unemployment headcount fell but macro growth weakened. Set an 80% interval of +/-0.2 percentage points around 6.3, giving 6.1 to 6.5.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153836:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z.6\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153837:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-17T02-11-36Z.euro-area-unemployment-rate-may-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-17t02-11-36z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153988:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.0\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153989:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153996:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.1\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2153997:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2154000:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"Japan's unemployment rate is a compact labour-market slack target for wage, consumption, and monetary-policy forecasts. This target resolves on 2026-06-30 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~1 month lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, wage pressure questions.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2154004:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00.2\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2154005:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06T05-41-31-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2154008:      \\\"publicText\\\": \\\"The April rate fell to 2.5% after March's 2.7%. Japan's unemployment rate usually moves slowly, so the agent holds the central estimate at 2.5% with a two-to-three-tenths uncertainty band.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2154012:      \\\"reasoningEventId\\\": \\\"reasoning.run.japan-unemployment-rate-may-2026.2026-06-06