itecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272099:            \\\"Base-rate/reference-class step: one-month changes in the rounded unemployment rate are usually small, and the last five official monthly prints have stayed in a 4.3 to 4.4 range, with four of five at 4.3.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272108:            \\\"Forecast for June 2026 BLS CPS unemployment rate\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272109:            \\\"The target is the first-print, seasonally adjusted CPS unemployment rate for June 2026, not a later revised value. The official BLS Employment Situation release is the resolver.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272118:            \\\"The target is the first-print, seasonally adjusted CPS unemployment rate for June 2026, not a later revised value. The official BLS Employment Situation release is the resolver.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272128:            \\\"Counter-consideration: household-survey noise can move the rounded unemployment rate by 0.1 or 0.2 points even when payroll growth is solid, and long-term unemployment near 2.0 million leaves some upside risk.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272145:            \\\"Counter-consideration: household-survey noise can move the rounded unemployment rate by 0.1 or 0.2 points even when payroll growth is solid, and long-term unemployment near 2.0 million leaves some upside risk.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272154:            \\\"Forecast for June 2026 BLS CPS unemployment rate\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272155:            \\\"Counter-consideration: household-survey noise can move the rounded unemployment rate by 0.1 or 0.2 points even when payroll growth is solid, and long-term unemployment near 2.0 million leaves some upside risk.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272163:      \\\"judgeRunId\\\": \\\"judge.trace.run.unemployment-rate-june-2026.2026-06-21T15-07-35Z.unemployment-rate-june-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-21t15-07-35z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272164:      \\\"runId\\\": \\\"run.unemployment-rate-june-2026.2026-06-21T15-07-35Z.unemployment-rate-june-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-21t15-07-35z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272174:            \\\"Base-rate/reference class: one-month moves in the rounded unemployment rate are usually small, and the immediate recent reference class is especially persistent: five latest monthly values are all between 4.3 and 4.4, with four of five at 4.3.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272184:            \\\"Forecast for June 2026 BLS CPS unemployment rate\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272185:            \\\"The resolver is the first official BLS Employment Situation print for June 2026, using the seasonally adjusted civilian unemployment rate for people age 16 and over, rounded to one decimal percent.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272194:            \\\"The resolver is the first official BLS Employment Situation print for June 2026, using the seasonally adjusted civilian unemployment rate for people age 16 and over, rounded to one decimal percent.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272204:            \\\"The main upside risk is that the household survey can be noisy and BLS says the unemployment-rate monthly-change confidence interval is about plus or minus 0.3 percentage point near a 6.0 percent rate; a softer June household survey could round to 4.4 or 4.5 even if payrolls remain positive.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272205:            \\\"The main downside risk is continued strong labor demand: May payrolls rose 172,000, participation was steady at 61.8 percent, and the unemployment rate has held at 4.3 despite month-to-month changes in unemployment levels.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272223:            \\\"The main upside risk is that the household survey can be noisy and BLS says the unemployment-rate monthly-change confidence interval is about plus or minus 0.3 percentage point near a 6.0 percent rate; a softer June household survey could round to 4.4 or 4.5 even if payrolls remain positive.\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272224:            \\\"The main downside risk is continued strong labor demand: May payrolls rose 172,000, participation was steady at 61.8 percent, and the unemployment rate has held at 4.3 despite month-to-month changes in unemployment levels.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272233:            \\\"Forecast for June 2026 BLS CPS unemployment rate\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2272234:            \\\"The main upside risk is that the household survey can be noisy and BLS says the unemployment-rate monthly-change confidence interval is about plus or minus 0.3 percentage point near a 6.0 percent rate; a softer June household survey could round to 4.4 or 4.5 even if payrolls remain positive.\\\"\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2274339:      \\\"judgeRunId\\\": \\\"judge.pairwise.run.uk-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00.vs.run.uk-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026.2026-06-27T13-39-06Z.uk-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026-thesis-analyst-fast-2026-06-27t13-39-06z\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2274340:      \\\"batchId\\\": \\\"pairwise.uk-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2274341:      \\\"leftRunId\\\": \\\"run.uk-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026.2026-06-04T10-32-04-01-00\\\",\\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:22