rt_m / the corresponding euro-indicators release, total sex, age 15-74, unit percent of active population, rounded to one decimal. Use the first official print only; ignore later revisions to May 2026.\\\",\\n  \\\"dataPointId\\\": \\\"eurostat.une_rt_m.ea20.pc_act.sa.y15-74.t.2026-05.first_print\\\",\\n  \\\"historicalContext\\\": [\\n   {\\n    \\\"label\\\": \\\"2026-04 latest first print\\\",\\n    \\\"value\\\": 6.3\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"label\\\": \\\"2026-03\\\",\\n    \\\"value\\\": 6.3\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"label\\\": \\\"2026-02\\\",\\n    \\\"value\\\": 6.4\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"label\\\": \\\"2026-01\\\",\\n    \\\"value\\\": 6.3\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"label\\\": \\\"2025-04\\\",\\n    \\\"value\\\": 6.3\\n   }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"drivers\\\": [\\n   \\\"April euro area unemployment stable at 6.3%\\\",\\n   \\\"Recent monthly range tightly clustered at 6.3-6.4%\\\",\\n   \\\"Euro area unemployed persons fell by 84 thousand in April\\\",\\n   \\\"Q1 GDP fell 0.2%, raising mild upside risk\\\",\\n   \\\"Inflation and energy shock may slow hiring but layoffs are not yet visible\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sourceContext\\\": [\\n   \\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/en/web/products-euro-indicators/w/3-01062026-ap\\\",\\n   \\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/news/euro-indicators\\\",\\n   \\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/main/news/release-calendar\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"runAt\\\": \\\"2026-06-17T02:11:36Z\\\",\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": [\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"heading\\\",\\n    \\\"text\\\": \\\"Euro area unemployment rate, May 2026 first print\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"text\\\",\\n    \\\"text\\\": \\\"The target is Eurostat's first official May 2026 euro area seasonally adjusted unemployment rate, total sex and age 15-74, in percent. The April 2026 Eurostat release states the next unemployment release is on 2 July 2026, so that is the verified resolution date for the May 2026 first print.\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tool\\\": \\\"official.lookup\\\",\\n    \\\"call\\\": \\\"Opened Eurostat euro-indicators unemployment release dated 1 June 2026 for April 2026.\\\",\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"Fetched April 2026 euro area unemployment rate 6.3%, March 2026 6.3%, April 2025 6.3%, and EU April 2026 6.0%.\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tool\\\": \\\"official.lookup\\\",\\n    \\\"call\\\": \\\"Read Eurostat table in the April 2026 unemployment release for recent euro area totals.\\\",\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"Fetched euro area rates: Apr-25 6.3, Jan-26 6.3, Feb-26 6.4, Mar-26 6.3, Apr-26 6.3; fetched unemployed persons: Apr-26 11075 thousand and Mar-26 11159 thousand.\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tool\\\": \\\"official.lookup\\\",\\n    \\\"call\\\": \\\"Checked Eurostat euro-indicators listing for nearby macro releases and publication schedule context.\\\",\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"Fetched official listing values: GDP Q1 2026 down 0.2% in euro area, employment Q1 2026 up 0.1%, May 2026 euro area inflation flash 3.2%, April 2026 retail trade down 0.4%.\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tool\\\": \\\"official.lookup\\\",\\n    \\\"call\\\": \\\"Opened Eurostat release calendar page for release-calendar provenance.\\\",\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"Fetched calendar note that the release calendar uses Europe/Luxembourg time zone and the April unemployment release shows Next release: 2 July 2026.\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"text\\\",\\n    \\\"text\\\": \\\"Base rate/reference class: monthly euro area unemployment rates usually move slowly at one-decimal precision; the last five official points shown for the euro area are 6.3, 6.3, 6.4, 6.3, and 6.3, making 6.3 the modal and median recent print.\\\"\\n   },\\n   {\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"text\\\",\\n    \\\"text\\\": \\\"The April level is stable year-on-year and month-on-month, while the number of euro area unemployed